{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_dead_letters_dead_letters", "label": "Dead letters", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/dead-letters.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_dead_letters_deadletter", "label": "DeadLetter", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/dead-letters.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A message the system could not deliver - a tell to a stopped ref, a selection that resolved to nothing, a behavior answering unhandled, a singleton with no host - wrapped and published on the event stream. That is the whole default behaviour: the framework does not log dead letters, DeadLetterRef holds no logger, so if nothing subscribes the letter is gone. Every letter names its recipient, which is what the filters and replay are built on."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_dead_letters_deadletterqueue", "label": "Dead-letter queue", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/dead-letters.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Always exists and by default keeps nothing. memory keeps a bounded ring, persistent adds an append-only journal log that survives a restart. list returns entries newest first, narrowed by an optional filter, and recipient matches a path or its subtree."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_dead_letters_deadletterqueueoptions", "label": "DeadLetterQueueOptions", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/dead-letters.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The same knobs as the HOCON block - store, max entries, retention and max replays - when you build the queue yourself."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_dead_letters_dead_letter_replay", "label": "Dead-letter replay", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/dead-letters.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Resolves the recipient path again rather than reusing a ref captured at failure time: the whole point is that the actor has come back since, at the same address as a new instance. Every outcome is named - replayed, unknown-entry, unresolved-recipient, degraded-payload, quarantined - so nothing fails quietly."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_dead_letters_degraded_payload", "label": "Degraded dead-letter payload", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/dead-letters.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The tagged-JSON encoder refuses functions, symbols, promises, weak collections and cycles rather than corrupting them silently, so a persistent queue keeps the provenance - class name and reason - instead of losing the letter. Such an entry cannot be replayed: there is nothing left to send."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_dead_letters_poison_message_quarantine", "label": "Poison messages cannot grow the queue", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/dead-letters.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A replayed message that dead-letters again comes back as the same entry with a higher replay count, not as a new one. Without that, an operator or a script retrying a message the recipient simply cannot handle would add an entry per attempt while every individual attempt still looked like a first. Past the limit the letter is quarantined and replay refuses it."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_dead_letters_dead_letter_durability", "label": "Dead-letter queue durability", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/dead-letters.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The persistence stream is derived from the system name, so two systems sharing one journal keep separate queues. Writes are issued as letters arrive and settled twice during coordinated shutdown - once before the system terminates and again after the actor tree is down, because the teardown itself produces dead letters after the last phase has run. A hard kill can still lose in-flight writes: this is a diagnostic record, not a transactional outbox."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_dead_letters_store_is_storage_not_strategy", "label": "store is a storage decision, not a failure strategy", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/dead-letters.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "What a projection should do when a handler throws is its recovery strategy; once it has skipped an event it publishes a dead letter, and this setting decides whether anything keeps it. The two compose - neither replaces the other."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_dead_letters_mailbox_drops_are_not_dead_letters", "label": "Mailbox drops are not dead letters", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/dead-letters.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A message discarded by a bounded or priority mailbox never becomes a dead letter at all: the drop seam reports a reason and never the envelope, so there is nothing to capture. The overflow shows up in the mailbox-dropped counter and nowhere else."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_dead_letters_dead_letters", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_dead_letters_deadletter", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/dead-letters.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_dead_letters_dead_letters", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_dead_letters_deadletterqueue", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/dead-letters.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_dead_letters_dead_letters", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_dead_letters_deadletterqueueoptions", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/dead-letters.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_dead_letters_dead_letters", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_dead_letters_dead_letter_replay", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/dead-letters.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_dead_letters_dead_letters", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_dead_letters_degraded_payload", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/dead-letters.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_dead_letters_dead_letters", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_dead_letters_poison_message_quarantine", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/dead-letters.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_dead_letters_dead_letters", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_dead_letters_dead_letter_durability", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/dead-letters.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_dead_letters_dead_letters", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_dead_letters_store_is_storage_not_strategy", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/dead-letters.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_dead_letters_dead_letters", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_dead_letters_mailbox_drops_are_not_dead_letters", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/dead-letters.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_dead_letters_degraded_payload", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_dead_letters_deadletterqueue", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/dead-letters.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_dead_letters_poison_message_quarantine", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_dead_letters_dead_letter_replay", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/dead-letters.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_dead_letters_dead_letter_durability", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_dead_letters_deadletterqueue", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/conte